    "**App icons instead of menu bar previews:** %@ shows an item’s app icon when it can’t capture the item, including when Screen Recording is off. Turn on Screen Recording to see the real icons. If an item is missing entirely, try relaunching %@." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "**App icons instead of menu bar previews:** %1$@ shows an item’s app icon when it can’t capture the item, including when Screen Recording is off. Turn on Screen Recording to see the real icons. If an item is missing entirely, try relaunching %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "**App icons instead of menu bar previews:** Thaw uses an app-icon fallback when a usable capture is unavailable, including when Screen Recording permission is off. The fallback is intentional; an item disappearing entirely still needs investigation." : {

    },
    "**Apps that need their own update:** macOS 27 changed how menu bar items are published, and an app built against the older behavior can sit in the wrong place, refuse to hide, or show no icon. f.lux behaves this way today. The fix has to come from the app's own developer; %@ cannot correct it from the outside. Check for an update to that app." : {

    },
    "**Apps that need their own update:** macOS 27 changed how menu bar items are published, and an app built against the older behavior can sit in the wrong place, refuse to hide, or show no icon. f.lux behaves this way today. The fix has to come from the app's own developer; Thaw cannot correct it from the outside." : {

    },
    "**Control Center items assigned to Hidden are switched off, not hidden:** Wi‑Fi, Bluetooth and other Control Center modules in Hidden or Always Hidden are turned off in macOS, and they do not come back when the section is revealed. Move them to Visible to show them again." : {

    },
    "**Several items from one app:** some apps’ menu bar items cannot be hidden independently with the current macOS 27 mechanism. An item assigned to Hidden can remain visible when another item from the same app is assigned to Visible. #1125" : {

    },
    "**Several items from one app:** some apps’ menu bar items cannot be hidden independently with the current macOS 27 mechanism. An item assigned to Hidden can remain visible when another item from the same app is assigned to Visible. To hide them, put all of that app’s items in the same section." : {

    },
    "**Some Control Center items assigned to Hidden are switched off, not hidden:** AirDrop, Focus, Now Playing and Fast User Switching in Hidden or Always Hidden are turned off in macOS, and they do not come back when the section is revealed. Move them to Visible to show them again. Wi‑Fi and Bluetooth hide and reveal like other items." : {

    },
    "**Spacing changes:** applying spacing can restart menu bar apps so they load the new value. Each app can also add its own padding, so the same setting does not guarantee identical visible gaps." : {

    },
